e,"_score_p_tbv":32.7,"_gate_mult_vs_hist":0.23026601596828744,"_gp_mult_vs_hist":false,"_score_mult_vs_hist":51.3,"_gate_fcf_yield":0.06739689922477456,"_gp_fcf_yield":true,"_score_fcf_yield":41.7,"_gate_int_coverage":7.955816079942525,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":36.6,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":-0.0008411939821837966,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":88.9,"_gate_accruals":-0.042159553386615936,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":53.3,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.05174129753268555,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":99.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.02641416973419347,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":67.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":0.083752217644246,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":41.9,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.21642978491127082,"_gp_roic_consistency":true,"_score_roic_consistency":63.9,"_gate_incr_roic":0.13754864416209805,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":62.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.1693294398385925,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":89.8,"_gate_pool_share":-0.006212490243135971,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":37.5,"_gate_rev_durability":0.08845739172659606,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":69.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.04846114056015627,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":49.2,"_gate_margins":0.007138840545780412,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":57.1,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.015278114711417733,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":28.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0008559119754463218,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":48.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.011887930441044867,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":80.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.00964,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"McGrath RentCorp operates as a business-to-business rental company in the United States and internationally. The company also engages in renting and selling relocatable modular buildings, portable storage containers, and electronic test equipment. The company operates through four segments: Mobile Modular, Portable Storage, TRS-RenTelco, and Enviroplex. The Mobile Modular segment rents and sells modular buildings designed for use as classrooms, temporary offices adjacent to existing facilities, sales offices, construction field offices, restroom buildings, health care clinics, childcare facilities, office spaces, and various other purposes. The Portable Storage segment offers steel containers, such as storage and office containers, to provide temporary storage solutions to construction, retail, commercial and industrial, energy and petrochemical, manufacturing, education, and healthcare markets. The TRS-RenTelco segment rents and sells general purpose electronic test equipment, such as oscilloscopes, amplifiers, analyzers, signal source, and power source test equipment primarily for the aerospace, defense, electronics, industrial, research, and semiconductor industries. This segment also provides communications test equipment, including network and transmission test equipment for various fiber, copper, and wireless networks to the manufacturers of communications equipment and products, electrical and communications installation contractors, field technicians, and service providers. The Enviroplex segment manufactures and sells portable classrooms directly to public school districts and other educational institutions in California. The company was incorporated in 1979 and is based in Livermore, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Philip B. Hawkins | President, CEO & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $917,579 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $723K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $162K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["McGrath RentCorp is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.1B market cap on $944M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 8% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 46%.","The business throws off $211M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 22 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.64\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 8.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.3\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.0021874474171283964},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $7.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 17% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","35 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Gross margin tops the Industrials peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(MGRC) as a Liquidity Pulse for Institutional Tactics","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/MGRC_as_a_Liquidity_Pulse_for_Institutional_Tactics_111226122001_1794504001.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794504001.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"S&P Index Addition Might Change The Case For Investing In McGrath RentCorp (MGRC)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-mgrc/mcgrath-rentcorp/news/sp-index-addition-might-change-the-case-for-investing-in-mcg","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794476178.008,"origin":"